1.	Introduction 

The objective of this project is to achieve a fully automated Nose Clip inspection line that integrates into the current Fanuc a-S100i (125T) machine in the clean room environment. This project aims to eliminate the need for any full-time inspection operators for the nose clips, instead relying on the Keyence VS-L camera system to check, categorise, and store good/defective part data onto a local FTP server. This line will also integrate an automated sorting system which uses the camera output signal to physically separate good/defective parts. 

2.	Scope

This project covers the design, implementation, and validation of an automated inspection and sorting system for plastic nose clips produced by the Fanuc a-S100i (125T) injection moulding machine within the cleanroom environment. The scope includes the following key elements

In Scope:
•	Integration of Keyence VS-L1600CX vision system for defect detection and part categorisation.
•	Design and installation of a backlit conveyor system compatible with the ES-1000II Star robot.
•	Development of an automated sorting mechanism triggered by camera output signals.
•	Development of an automated defective part reject system.
•	Configuration of data storage and traceability through a local FTP server.
•	Operator interface and control panel (e.g. for job traveller number/program change or manual override)

Out of Scope:
•	Modifications to the injection moulding machine or mould tools.
•	Changes to existing robot (Star ES-1000II) beyond control software.
•	System scalability to different part types beyond design considerations.

